---
title: Frozen Fruit Salad
author: Mary Arntson
category: Salads
source: Loving Memories of Mildred
---

@pineapple tidbits{1%med can} - drained (save syrup)
@sliced strawberries{1.5%c} (or 2 packages of frozen)
@miniature marshmallows{2%c}
@pecans{1/4%c}
@unflavored gelatin{1%envelop}
@pineapple syrup (cold){2%Tbsp}
@salad dressing{1/4%c}
@whipped cream{1%c}

Drain pineapple and save the syrup. Combine pineapple, strawberries, marshmallows and pecans. Soften gelatin in 2 Tbsp cold syrup - dissolve that in hot syrup and add to fruit mixture. Fold salad dressing into whipped cream. Fold that into fruit and nut mixture. Fill paper baking cups and freeze. 16 servings
